          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-20485 misc: use LLVM automatic reference counting",
        "message": "LU-20485 misc: use LLVM automatic reference counting\n\nWe might be able to use LLVM's automatic reference counting [1] to\nfind ref count bugs in our kernel code. While this feature was\noriginally designed for Objective-C, the annotations work fine\non C. I was able to discover a few small bugs with this. This\nwarrants more discussion with the upstream Linux/LLVM maintainers\nto understand if there is a path to adoption in the Linux kernel.\n\nThis is a PoC.\n\n[1] https://clang.llvm.org/docs/AutomaticReferenceCounting.html\n\nTest-Parameters: ignore\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ifdfe04acfbb3e9416162dd65633a153b973c43a3\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
